# GUAI server, Docker image (publishes to ghcr.io on version tags), and
# Pebble watchface/app (attached to the GitHub release) — see spec/operations.md.
# Compose pulls the published image; override for local builds:
#   GUAI_IMAGE=guai:local
GUAI_IMAGE=ghcr.io/divin/guai:1.0.0
TZ=Europe/Berlin
GUAI_SYNC_TOKEN=change-me-to-at-least-16-chars
GUAI_DB_PATH=/data/guai.sqlite3
GUAI_WEATHER_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60
# Server surface per instance (docker-compose sets these per service):
#   full     — everything in one instance (default; the compose "guai" service)
#   device   — only the token-protected endpoints for watchface/app; expose THIS
#              instance via reverse proxy/TLS ("guai-device" service). Runs no
#              scheduler and no migrations; pair it with a full/internal instance.
#   internal — dashboard + management APIs + frontend, scheduler, migrations; LAN only.
# GUAI_SERVER_MODE=full
# GUAI_STATIC_DIR=/app/static
# PUSHOVER_TOKEN=
# PUSHOVER_USER=
